It seems like you want to make all the cart operations (add, plus, minus, remove) work without reloading the current page. To achieve this, you can make use of JavaScript/jQuery and AJAX to call the appropriate Django views without requiring a page refresh.

Here's an example of how you can modify your JavaScript/jQuery code to handle the button clicks:

```javascript
$(document).ready(function() {
  // Add to cart button
  $('.btn-add-to-cart').click(function(e) {
    e.preventDefault(); // prevent form submission

    // Call the add-to-cart view
    $.get("/add-to-cart", { prod_id: $(this).data("product-id") }, function(data) {
      // Update the UI or display a success message
    });
  });

  // Plus cart button
  $('.plus-cart').click(function(e) {
    e.preventDefault();

    // Call the plus-cart view
    $.get("/plus-cart", { prod_id: $(this).attr("pid") }, function(data) {
      // Update the UI
      $("#quantity").text(data.quantity);
    });
  });

  // Minus cart button
  $('.minus-cart').click(function(e) {
    e.preventDefault();

    // Check if the current quantity is 1, then call the remove-cart view
    if ($("#quantity").text() == 1) {
      $.get("/remove-cart", { prod_id: $(this).attr("pid") }, function(data) {
        // Update the UI or display a success message
      });
    } else {
      // Call the minus-cart view
      $.get("/minus-cart", { prod_id: $(this).attr("pid") }, function(data) {
        // Update the UI
        $("#quantity").text(data.quantity);
      });
    }
  });

  // Remove cart button (if needed)
  $('.remove-cart').click(function(e) {
    e.preventDefault();

    // Call the remove-cart view
    $.get("/remove-cart", { prod_id: $(this).data("product-id") }, function(data) {
      // Update the UI or display a success message
    });
  });
});
```

In your HTML, add the `btn-add-to-cart` class to the Add to Cart button and use `data-product-id` attribute to store the product ID:

```html
<button
  type="submit"
  class="btn btn-success shadow px-5 py-2 btn-add-to-cart"
  data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
>
  Add to Cart
</button>
```

This way, all the operations will be performed without reloading the page, and you'll only need to update the user interface (UI) accordingly in the JavaScript callbacks. Make sure you have jQuery included in your project for the AJAX calls to work.

