To randomize the order of values in an associative array in PHP, you can use the `shuffle()` function, which shuffles the elements of an array in place. Here's an example:

```php
<?php
$assocArr = array(
    "name" => "John",
    "age" => 30,
    "city" => "New York"
);

// Get the values of the associative array
$values = array_values($assocArr);

// Shuffle the values
shuffle($values);

// Create a new associative array with the shuffled values
$randomizedArr = array_combine(array_keys($assocArr), $values);

// Output the shuffled associative array
var_dump($randomizedArr);
?>
```

The `array_values()` function is used to get the values of the associative array and `shuffle()` function is used to shuffle the values. `array_combine()` function is then used to create a new associative array with the shuffled values and the original keys. 

This will output a randomized associative array with the values shuffled in random order.

To convert a YTD (YouTube video) file to multiple PNG images, we'll use three main components:

1. Download the YouTube video using youtube-dl.
2. Convert the video to images using FFmpeg.
3. Create a C# Console Program to automate the process.

Before we begin, make sure to install youtube-dl and FFmpeg on your machine.

#### Step 1: Install youtube-dl

- Download the youtube-dl executable from the official repository (https://github.com/ytdl-org/youtube-dl/releases).
- Extract the zip file and add the location of youtube-dl.exe to your PATH environment variable.

#### Step 2: Install FFmpeg

- Download FFmpeg from the official website (https://ffmpeg.org/download.html).
- Extract the zip file and add the location of the FFmpeg 'bin' folder to your PATH environment variable.

Now that youtube-dl and FFmpeg are installed, let's create the C# Console Program.

#### Step 3: Create a New C# Console Project

1. Open Visual Studio and create a new C# Console App (.NET Core) project.
2. Add a new class called "YtdToPngConverter" to the project.

#### Step 4: Write the C# Code

Open the "YtdToPngConverter" class file and add the following code:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Diagnostics;
using System.IO;

public class YtdToPngConverter
{
    public string YoutubeDlPath { get; set; }
    public string FFmpegPath { get; set; }
    public string OutputFolder { get; set; }

    public void DownloadVideo(string url)
    {
        var processStartInfo = new ProcessStartInfo
        {
            FileName = YoutubeDlPath,
            Arguments = $"-f mp4 -o \"%(title)s.%(ext)s\" {url}",
            RedirectStandardOutput = true,
            UseShellExecute = false,
            CreateNoWindow = true
        };

        var process = new Process { StartInfo = processStartInfo };
        process.Start();
        process.WaitForExit();
    }

    public void ConvertVideoToImages(string inputFilePath)
    {
        Directory.CreateDirectory(OutputFolder);

        var processStartInfo = new ProcessStartInfo
        {
            FileName = FFmpegPath,
            Arguments = $"-i \"{inputFilePath}\" -vf fps=1 \"{Path.Combine(OutputFolder, "output%03d.png")}\"",
            RedirectStandardOutput = true,
            UseShellExecute = false,
            CreateNoWindow = true
        };

        var process = new Process { StartInfo = processStartInfo };
        process.Start();
        process.WaitForExit();
    }
}
```

Now, in the "Program.cs" file, add the following code:

```csharp
using System;

namespace YtdToPng
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            Console.WriteLine("Enter the YouTube video URL:");
            string url = Console.ReadLine();

            Console.WriteLine("Enter the output folder path for PNG images:");
            string outputPath = Console.ReadLine();

            YtdToPngConverter converter = new YtdToPngConverter
            {
                YoutubeDlPath = "youtube-dl.exe",
                FFmpegPath = "ffmpeg.exe",
                OutputFolder = outputPath
            };

            Console.WriteLine("Downloading video...");
            converter.DownloadVideo(url);

            string videoFileName = $"{url.Substring(url.LastIndexOf("=") + 1)}.mp4"; // Assuming the video format is MP4.
            Console.WriteLine("Converting video to images...");
            converter.ConvertVideoToImages(videoFileName);

            Console.WriteLine("Process completed. Press any key to exit.");
            Console.ReadKey();
        }
    }
}
```

#### Step 5: Build and Run the Program

1. Build the solution in Visual Studio.
2. Open a Command Prompt and navigate to the build directory.
3. Run the program, enter the YouTube video URL, and output folder path for the PNG images.

The program will download the video and then convert it to PNG images in the specified output folder.

