3. Next, I will write the Rust code that takes input parameters (such as name, award, date, etc.) and generates a dynamic PDF certificate using the pdf-generation library. 

4. After that, I will create a simple HTTP API using the HTTP server library that accepts input parameters via HTTP POST request, calls the Rust function to generate PDF certificates, and sends the generated PDF file as a response. 

5. Finally, I will test the API locally to ensure that it works as expected and generates dynamic PDF certificates with given input parameters. 

