2. Add Pellet to the Jena class path: Once Pellet is installed, you need to add its jars to the Java class path. You can do this by adding the following line to your Java program:

   Class.forName("com.clarkparsia.pellet.owlapiv3.PelletReasonerFactory");

3. Create an instance of the Pellet reasoner: The Pellet reasoner can be created by calling the factory method:

   Reasoner reasoner = PelletReasonerFactory.getInstance().create();

4. Attach the reasoner to a Jena model: Once you have created the reasoner, you can attach it to your Jena model by calling the method:

   InfModel infmodel = ModelFactory.createInfModel(reasoner, model);

   Here "model" is your Jena RDF model, and "infmodel" is the inferred model that contains the results of the reasoning.

5. Use the inferred model: Once the Pellet reasoner is attached to your Jena model, you can use the inferred model to query and reason over it.

