This code iterates through each command in the drawlist and increments the `object_count` for each non-callback command. Finally, the count is displayed using a `ImGui::Text` command. 

This approach doesn't differentiate between different types of objects (e.g. circles, rectangles, lines), but simply counts the number of non-callback commands, which should give you the total number of objects being drawn.

Yes, it is possible to count the number of specific objects being drawn within an ImGui drawlist by checking for the corresponding draw commands and incrementing a counter for each one. Here's an example of how to count the number of circles being drawn:

```cpp
int circle_count = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < draw_list->CmdBuffer.Size; i++)
{
    const ImDrawCmd* cmd = &draw_list->CmdBuffer[i];
    if (cmd->UserCallback != nullptr)
    {
        // Handle custom user callbacks
    }
    else if (cmd->ElemCount > 0 && cmd->UserCallback == nullptr)
    {
        const ImDrawIdx* idx_buffer = draw_list->IdxBuffer.Data + cmd->IdxOffset;
        const ImDrawVert* vtx_buffer = draw_list->VtxBuffer.Data + cmd->VtxOffset;
        for (int j = 0; j < cmd->ElemCount; j += 3)
        {
            ImDrawIdx idx0 = idx_buffer[j + 0];
            ImDrawIdx idx1 = idx_buffer[j + 1];
            ImDrawIdx idx2 = idx_buffer[j + 2];

            const ImVec2& v0 = vtx_buffer[idx0].pos;
            const ImVec2& v1 = vtx_buffer[idx1].pos;
            const ImVec2& v2 = vtx_buffer[idx2].pos;

            // Check if the vertices form a circle
            if (v0.x == v1.x && v0.y == v1.y && // Center vertex
                v1.x == v2.x && v1.y == v2.y)   // Two circumference vertices
            {
                circle_count++;
            }
        }
    }
}

ImGui::Text("Circle count: %d", circle_count);
```

This code iterates through each command in the drawlist and checks whether it is a `ImDrawCmd` element command. It then verifies whether the vertices of the triangle are circling around the same point. If so, it increments the `circle_count`. Finally, the count is displayed using a `ImGui::Text` command.

You can modify this code to count other types of drawn objects (e.g. rectangles, lines, text) by checking for their corresponding draw commands and vertex patterns.

