To make the `JLabel`s draggable, we add a `MouseListener` and a `MouseMotionListener` to the panel. In the `mousePressed` method of the `MouseListener`, we bring the `JLabel` that was clicked to the front by setting its component z-order to 0. In the `mouseDragged` method of the `MouseMotionListener`, we set the location of both `JLabel`s to the current mouse position, adjusted by the size of `label1`, so that `label2` follows `label1`.

With this code, you should be able to drag the `JLabel`s to any position of the full screen `JFrame` screen and their positions will stay in sync with the new dragged mouse position.

