        panel.setLayout(null);
        panel.setBackground(Color.WHITE);

        JLabel label1 = new JLabel(new ImageIcon("path/to/image1.png"));
        label1.setHorizontalAlignment(SwingConstants.CENTER);
        label1.setVerticalAlignment(SwingConstants.CENTER);
        label1.setSize(label1.getPreferredSize());
        label1.setLocation(new Point(100, 100));

        JLabel label2 = new JLabel(new ImageIcon("path/to/image2.png"));
        label2.setHorizontalAlignment(SwingConstants.CENTER);
        label2.setVerticalAlignment(SwingConstants.CENTER);
        label2.setSize(label2.getPreferredSize());
        label2.setLocation(new Point(500, 200));

        panel.add(label1);
        panel.add(label2);

        panel.addMouseListener(new MouseAdapter() {
            public void mousePressed(MouseEvent e) {
                if (e.getSource() instanceof JLabel) {
                    JLabel label = (JLabel) e.getSource();
                    label.getParent().setComponentZOrder(label, 0); // Bring label to front
                    selectedLabel = label; // Set selected label
                }
            }

            public void mouseReleased(MouseEvent e) {
                selectedLabel = null; // Clear selected label
            }
        });

        panel.addMouseMotionListener(new MouseAdapter() {
            public void mouseDragged(MouseEvent e) {
                if (selectedLabel != null) { // If a label is selected
                    selectedLabel.setLocation(e.getX() - selectedLabel.getWidth() / 2, e.getY() - selectedLabel.getHeight() / 2);
                }
            }
        });

        frame.add(panel);
        frame.setVisible(true);
    }
}
```

In this version of the code, we add a `selectedLabel` variable to keep track of which label is being dragged. When the `mousePressed` method is called, we check if the event source is a `JLabel` and set it as the selected label. When the `mouseReleased` method is called, we clear the selected label.

In the `mouseDragged` method, we check if there is a selected label and update its position accordingly. This allows the labels to be dragged independently of each other.

