To configure an ASP.NET Core web service to use TLS 1.2 via the `appsettings.json` configuration file, follow these steps:

1. Open the `appsettings.json` file in your ASP.NET Core project.

2. Add a new section for configuring the TLS options. For example:

   ```json
   "TlsOptions": {
     "Protocol": "Tls12"
   }
   ```

3. Configure the server to use the provided TLS options. Modify the `ConfigureServices` method in the `Startup.cs` file as follows:

   ```csharp
   using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Server.Kestrel.Core;

   public class Startup
   {
       // ...

       public void ConfigureServices(IServiceCollection services)
       {
           // ...
           services.Configure<KestrelServerOptions>(Configuration.GetSection("TlsOptions"));
           // ...
       }

       // ...
   }
   ```

4. Configure Kestrel to use the provided TLS options. Modify the `ConfigureServices` method in the `Startup.cs` file as follows:

   ```csharp
   public void Configure(IApplicationBuilder app, IWebHostEnvironment env)
   {
       // ...
       var tlsOptions = app.ApplicationServices.GetService<IOptions<KestrelServerOptions>>().Value;
       tlsOptions.ConfigureEndpointDefaults(opts => opts.Protocols = tlsOptions.Protocols | SslProtocols.Tls12);
       // ...
   }
   ```

5. Build and run your ASP.NET Core web service.

By following these steps, your ASP.NET Core web service will be configured to use TLS 1.2 as specified in the `appsettings.json` configuration file.

To configure an ASP.NET Core web service to use TLS 1.2 via the `appsettings.json` configuration file in .NET 7, you can follow these steps:

1. Open the `appsettings.json` file in your ASP.NET Core project.

2. Add a new section for configuring the TLS options. For example:

   ```json
   "TlsOptions": {
     "Protocol": "Tls12"
   }
   ```

3. Modify the `Program.cs` file to use the `ConfigureAppConfiguration` method to configure the TLS options from `appsettings.json`. Update the `CreateHostBuilder` method as follows:

   ```csharp
   using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Server.Kestrel.Core;

   public class Program
   {
       public static void Main(string[] args)
       {
           var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);
           // ...
           builder.ConfigureAppConfiguration((hostingContext, config) =>
           {
               var tlsOptions = config.GetSection("TlsOptions").Get<TlsOptions>();
               builder.ConfigureServices((_, services) =>
               {
                   services.Configure<KestrelServerOptions>(options =>
                   {
                       options.ConfigureEndpointDefaults(ep =>
                       {
                           ep.Protocols = tlsOptions.Protocols;
                       });
                   });
               });
           });
           // ...
           var app = builder.Build();
           // ...
           app.Run();
       }
   }
   ```

4. Create a `TlsOptions` class to hold the TLS configuration settings. Add a new file called `TlsOptions.cs` with the following code:

   ```csharp
   using System.Security.Authentication;

   public class TlsOptions
   {
       public SslProtocols Protocols { get; set; }
   }
   ```

5. Build and run your ASP.NET Core web service.

By following these steps, your ASP.NET Core web service will be configured to use TLS 1.2 as specified in the `appsettings.json` configuration file in .NET 7.

