}
```

In this updated code, `sizeof(ctxt)` returns the size of the structure type itself, not an instance of it. The `size` variable then stores this size value, which is printed using `printf`.

Please note that the size reported by `sizeof` includes any padding or alignment requirements of the structure members, so it may be larger than the sum of the sizes of the individual members.

