To create an HTML5 button for Bluetooth functionality, you can use the Web Bluetooth API. Here's an example of how you can create a button that allows the user to connect to a nearby Bluetooth device:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>

<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Bluetooth Button</title>
</head>

<body>
  <button id="connectButton">Connect to Bluetooth Device</button>

  <script>
    // Check if the Web Bluetooth API is available in the browser
    if ('bluetooth' in navigator) {
      const connectButton = document.getElementById('connectButton');

      // Add event listener for button click
      connectButton.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        try {
          // Request Bluetooth device for connection
          const device = await navigator.bluetooth.requestDevice({
            // Filters for desired Bluetooth device
            filters: [{
              services: ['your_service_uuid']
            }]
          });

          // Do something with the connected Bluetooth device
          console.log('Connected to: ', device.name);
          // Perform the required operations with the device

        } catch (error) {
          // Handle any errors during the connection
          console.error('Error: ', error);
        }
      });
    } else {
      console.log('Web Bluetooth is not supported in this browser.');
    }
  </script>
</body>

</html>
```

In this code example, a button with the id `connectButton` is created. When the button is clicked, it triggers an event listener that uses the `navigator.bluetooth.requestDevice` method to prompt the user to select a Bluetooth device. The chosen device can be accessed through the `device` object, allowing you to perform operations specific to the connected Bluetooth device.

Note that you will need to replace `'your_service_uuid'` with the actual UUID of the Bluetooth service you want to connect to.

To call a function from a package in Flutter, you first need to import the package. Then, you can directly call the function using its name.

