    // Check if the task creation was successful
    if( taskHandle != NULL )
    {
        // Task created successfully
    }
    else
    {
        // Failed to create the task
    }
}
```

In the above example, we define a task function vMyTask() and use the xTaskCreate() function to create an instance of this task. The first parameter is the task function, followed by the task name, stack size, task parameters, task priority, and a pointer to the task handle.

Note that you need to pass a pointer to a task handle (TaskHandle_t) to xTaskCreate() function if you want to check if the task creation was successful.

While there is no direct equivalent of kthread_create() in FreeRTOS, the xTaskCreate() function can be used to create tasks dynamically and achieve similar functionality.

