To keep the ampersand (&) symbol in Java, you need to escape it by using the backslash (\). The backslash is used to escape special characters in Java and prevent them from being treated as operators or control characters.

Here is an example of how to keep the ampersand symbol:

```java
public class Main {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    String text = "This is a sample text with & symbol";
    System.out.println(text);

    // Alternatively, you can use the escape character as a reference
    String escapedText = "This is a sample text with \\& symbol";
    System.out.println(escapedText);
  }
}
```

In the above example, we have two strings: `text` and `escapedText`. The first string contains the ampersand symbol directly, while the second string uses the backslash to escape the ampersand symbol.

