To rotate a rectangle drawn using graphics in C#, you can use the Graphics class and the RotateTransform method. Here's an example of rotating a rectangle by a specified angle:

1. First, create a new Windows Forms Application project in Visual Studio.

2. Open the Form1.cs file and add the following code inside the Paint event:

```csharp
private void Form1_Paint(object sender, PaintEventArgs e)
{
    // Create a Graphics object from the Form's handle
    Graphics g = this.CreateGraphics();

    // Specify the rectangle's properties
    int x = 50;
    int y = 50;
    int width = 100;
    int height = 50;
    int angle = 45; // Rotate by 45 degrees

    // Create a rectangle object
    Rectangle rect = new Rectangle(x, y, width, height);

    // Rotate the graphics object by the specified angle around the center of the rectangle
    g.TranslateTransform(rect.Left + (rect.Width / 2), rect.Top + (rect.Height / 2));
    g.RotateTransform(angle);
    g.TranslateTransform(-rect.Left - (rect.Width / 2), -rect.Top - (rect.Height / 2));

    // Draw the rotated rectangle
    g.DrawRectangle(Pens.Black, rect);
}
```

3. In the Form1 constructor, add the following code to enable the Paint event:

```csharp
