To add tracking and spacing to a text in Jetpack Compose Kotlin, you can use the `AnnotatedString` along with `RangedAnnotation`. Here's an example of how you can achieve this:

```kotlin
import androidx.compose.foundation.layout.Column
import androidx.compose.runtime.Composable
import androidx.compose.ui.Modifier
import androidx.compose.ui.graphics.Color
import androidx.compose.ui.text.AnnotatedString
import androidx.compose.ui.text.SpanStyle
import androidx.compose.ui.text.buildAnnotatedString
import androidx.compose.ui.text.withStyle
import androidx.compose.ui.tooling.preview.Preview
import androidx.compose.ui.unit.sp

@Composable
fun TrackingAndSpacingText() {
    Column(modifier = Modifier.padding(16.dp)) {
        TextWithTrackingAndSpacing("Hello World", spacing = 8.sp, tracking = 0.2f)
    }
}

@Composable
fun TextWithTrackingAndSpacing(text: String, spacing: Spacing, tracking: Float) {
    val annotatedString = buildAnnotatedString {
        withStyle(SpanStyle(fontSize = 18.sp, letterSpacing = tracking.sp)) {
            append(text)
            append(' ') // Add some spacing
        }

        addStyle(
            style = SpanStyle(color = Color.Red, fontSize = 24.sp),
            start = 0,
            end = text.length
        ) // Add some color, you can customize it as per your requirement
    }

    Text(
        text = annotatedString,
        lineHeight = spacing
    )
}

@Preview
@Composable
fun PreviewTrackingAndSpacingText() {
    TrackingAndSpacingText()
}
```

In this example, we create a `TextWithTrackingAndSpacing` composable that takes the text, spacing, and tracking as parameters. We use `buildAnnotatedString` to create an `AnnotatedString` and apply the desired styles to the text. We add a `SpanStyle` with the provided tracking value and append the text and some spacing using `append` and `append(' ')`.

Finally, we use the `Text` composable to display the formatted text, and we pass the `Spacing` value as the `lineHeight` parameter to control the spacing between the lines.

Note: Make sure to include the required dependencies in your project's `build.gradle` file to use Jetpack Compose, like `implementation "androidx.compose.ui:ui:x.x.x"` and `implementation "androidx.compose.foundation:foundation:x.x.x"`.

