void wake_up(WaitQueueHead_t* wq_head) {
    xSemaphoreTake(wq_head->mutex, portMAX_DELAY);

    while (wq_head->first != NULL) {
        struct WaitQueueEntry* next = wq_head->first->next;
        TaskHandle_t taskHandle = wq_head->first->taskHandle;

        if (next == NULL) {
            wq_head->last = NULL;
        }

        wq_head->first = next;

        xSemaphoreGive(wq_head->mutex);
        xTaskNotifyGive(taskHandle); // Use task notification to wake up the task

        // Take mutex again for next iteration
        xSemaphoreTake(wq_head->mutex, portMAX_DELAY);
    }

    xSemaphoreGive(wq_head->mutex);
}
```

This modified `wake_up` function iterates through the wait queue and wakes up each task by issuing task notifications. It updates the first and last pointers accordingly and releases the mutex between iterations to allow other operations on the wait queue.

By making these changes, the `wake_up` function will now wake up all tasks in the wait queue, ensuring that all tasks waiting on the condition are notified.

