If you want to supply a string to clap with a default value, you can use the `.default_value()` method provided by the clap library. Here's an example of how you can do that:

```rust
use clap::{App, Arg};

fn main() {
    let matches = App::new("MyApp")
        .arg(
            Arg::new("input")
                .about("input string")
                .required(false)
                .default_value("default value")
                .takes_value(true),
        )
        .get_matches();

    let input = matches.value_of("input").unwrap();
    println!("Input: {}", input);
}
