To convert a non-string value in a JSON object to a string, you can use the `std::to_string()` function to convert it to a string representation. Here's an example:

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <nlohmann/json.hpp>

int main() {
    nlohmann::json data = R"(
        {
            "metricValue": 42
        }
    )"_json;

    std::string dummy;
    dummy = std::to_string(data["metricValue"].get<int>());

    std::cout << dummy << std::endl;

    return 0;
}
```

