In this example, the threaded_irq_handler() is the threaded interrupt handler function. It performs the necessary processing in process context and then returns IRQ_HANDLED to indicate that the interrupt has been handled.

When calling request_threaded_irq(), you would pass this threaded_irq_handler() function as the thread_fn argument.

