public String messageProducer(String message, String requestQueueName) {
    try {
        Connection connection = tibJmsConnectionFactory.createConnection();
        Session session = connection.createSession(Session.AUTO_ACKNOWLEDGE);

        Destination requestQueue = session.createQueue(requestQueueName);
        Destination responseQueue = session.createQueue("ms.catenate.test.login.sync.response");

        MessageProducer producer = session.createProducer(requestQueue);
        connection.start();

        TextMessage textMessage = session.createTextMessage(message);
        textMessage.setStringProperty("SoapAction", "/LoginService/login");
        textMessage.setJMSReplyTo(responseQueue);
        producer.send(textMessage);
        System.out.println("---Message sent");

        connection.close();
    } catch (JMSException e) {
        System.out.println("Error: " + e.getMessage());
        throw new RuntimeException(e);
    }
    return message;
}
```

In this updated code, the producer sets the `JMSReplyTo` property of the message to the response queue. The consumer listens to the request queue and sends the response message to the response queue specified in the `JMSReplyTo` property.

